  message: "DONE — dev ae67059b51. The scope statement this item specified is generated\ninto SECURITY.md by scripts/generate-security-md (not a governance file, as\nthe item noted).\n\nMERGED-TREE EVIDENCE, not \"the code landed\":\n  SECURITY.md:12  \"### What this audit covers\"\n  SECURITY.md:14  \"Scope: the installed CLI.\"\n  SECURITY.md:34  \"Read the claims below as CLAIMS UNDER TEST\"\n  generate-security-md --check -> \"OK: SECURITY.md is up to date.\"\nThe section renders BEFORE the measured-verdict table on purpose: a reader\nneeds to know what was examined before being told it came back 18 of 18\ninconclusive.\n\nWHAT IT STATES, matching this item's table: covered = the installed CLI\n(every claim takes a python cmd_* handler as its source). Uncovered, each\nnamed rather than left to inference = pytest inside the repo, git/agent\nhooks, CI, and hypergumbo ANALYSING a repo (rust-analyzer executing the\ntarget's build.rs).\n\nTHE THREE DISCLOSURES THIS ITEM ARGUED FOR, all present:\n  * conftest.py executes at COLLECTION, so --collect-only runs it with no\n    test selected; the root conftest subprocesses and re-execs BY DESIGN\n    (ADR-0010).\n  * WHICH THREAT MODEL. The audit discards test-sourced flows (WI-bifob) —\n    right for \"is the shipped tool safe to run\", backwards for \"is this repo\n    safe to run tests in\". The artifact now says which question it answers.\n  * The .md/.txt result is recorded as a CONFIGURATION fact revocable by one\n    line in pyproject.toml, NOT a structural guarantee. That is the honest\n    answer to the owner's originating question and the overclaim this\n    section exists to prevent.\n\nTESTS PIN CONTENT, NOT PROSE: six tests assert the covered context is named,\nevery uncovered context appears, collection-time execution is stated, the\nthreat-model sentence exists, and the configuration-not-structure wording\nsurvives. Rewording stays cheap; dropping a disclosure does not.\n\nSTILL THE OWNER'S, and deliberately not resolved here: whether a scope\nstatement is sufficient or whether any uncovered context should get claims\nof its own. That is a threat-model decision and part of the INV-dabuf\npackage.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR INV-sarum, which this item was flagged as gating: by\ndeclaring the SHIPPED-TOOL model, the scope statement settles that fork —\nproduction-scope the node census, parity with WI-bifob."  # cc86
